# Renault 15 two-door, 1972-1979.
#
# The Renault 15, the less sporting half of the 15/17 pair, on sale from 1972
# and built until August 1979. It shared the Renault 17's shell, wheelbase and
# door with a different front and rear, and was built as a variant of the 17
# master.
#
# Dimensions 4.255 x 1.640 x 1.310 m, wheelbase 2.440 m, as the 17. Source: the
# reference pack's notes, from the Renault 15/17 dimension box.
#
# What differs from the 17: a single wide rectangular grille with the badge and
# rectangular headlamps instead of the 17's twin round lamps and slim grille; a
# plain rear quarter instead of the louvred quarter; and the hatch with its
# spoiler, the segmented tail lamps and the rear bumper of the blue reference
# car. The roofline, door and wheels are the 17's.
#
# Shape reference: a brown 15 rear quarter, a blue 15 front three-quarter and
# the blue car from the rear left. The true side elevation of the model was
# rendered and checked for the side window band.
#
# Colours: no British-market names were established, so the objects carry plain
# names: yellow, red, white and blue. Weights yellow 3, red 3, white 2, blue 2,
# total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 155 km/h, the 1.3-litre car's quoted maximum. Comfort 50/255, on the
# line 180 + 1.5 x 50: a small, softly sprung family coupé. Classes 1,2.
#
# Dates are road presence: 1972 intro, retires staggered 1988-1991 on a
# sixteen- to nineteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/renault-15.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/renault-15.dae (122 objects). References:
# citycars/references/renault-15/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the carried-over cabin is slightly taller than the
# photographs and the comparison angles are approximate. At 128 px the single
# rectangular grille and the plain quarter distinguish the 15 from the 17.

obj=citycar
name=Renault15(Yellow)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1972
intro_month=1
retire_year=1991
retire_month=6
speed=155
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=50
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=255

